/-!
# The rank-two characteristic-two branch of Section 15.3

The local preparation constructs the component span, its genuine action
quotient and faithful binary representation. It proves `V ≤ Z(R)`,
quasisimplicity of the component image, the covering step for a two-group
center, the central-omega rank bound, and the conjugate-pair normalizer
contradiction shared by two of the block eliminations.

The remaining argument must establish the C.2.7 alternatives and eliminate
the nonbinary blocks (15.3.17–22), `L₃(2)` (15.3.23), and `L₄(2), L₅(2)`
(15.3.24). These results must apply to the actual smaller outside overgroups
used by the parabolic arguments. Theorem 15.3.13 is not yet established here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
printed pp.1125–1130 (PDF pp.1142–1147).
-/
